# Data layer

## Endpoints and tags

- Add endpoints to the area's slice with `xmsApi.injectEndpoints({ endpoints: (build) => ({ ... }), overrideExisting: false })` and export the hooks from it. Type both sides: `build.query<BillingPeriod[], string>`.
- Every query provides a tag and every mutation invalidates one. Build them with the slice's helper (`budgetTag(accountId)`, `billingTag(accountId)` in `redux/timeApi.ts`) so provider and invalidator cannot drift. A new tag type goes into `tagTypes` in `redux/api.ts`.
- Invalidate everything the write changes, not only the record it names: `logTicketTime` reloads the ticket's time, the timesheet, comp time, the contract position and the budget.
- Decide what a refusal reloads, and say why in a comment on the endpoint.
  - A refusal that means the view is behind (`stale_version`, `invalid_transition`) reloads anyway: `invalidatesTags: (_result, _error, { accountId }) => [billingTag(accountId)]` on `transitionBillingPeriod`.
  - A refusal that changed nothing reloads nothing: `(_result, error, { accountId }) => (error ? [] : [rateCardsTag(accountId)])` on `createRateCard`.
- A write to a versioned record sends the `version` the screen read: `patchEngagementBody(engagement, draft)` puts `engagement.version` first.

## Errors

- Read every error with `apiError(error)` from `lib/admin/api-error.ts` (`status`, `code`, `details`, `permission`, `requestId`). An area with its own codes adds a reader that keeps the extra fields its bodies carry (`capacityError` keeps `current`, `problems` and `keys`) and a describer that switches on `code` with `default: return describeError(error)`.
- Branch on `code`, never on message text or on the status alone.
  YES: `case "stale_version":`. NO: `if (String(error.data?.message).includes("version"))`.
- For an edit to a versioned record, take the handler from `useMutationErrors(refetch)` in `lib/admin/use-mutation-errors.ts`. On `stale_version` it toasts "Reloaded" and refetches, otherwise it toasts "Not saved", and it returns the parsed error for inline display. It words with the shared `describeError`, so a code only your area knows goes through your describer instead.

## Transport and polling

- No `fetch` in a component or a page; ESLint refuses it there. A JSON route is an endpoint. A file the reader downloads goes through `downloadFile` or `fetchDownload` in `lib/exports/download.ts`, with the path from the slice (`downloadFile({ url: billingExportPath(accountId, period.id, format) })`). A presigned link the API minted opens with `openExternal` (`security.mdc`).
- Poll with `pollingInterval: LIVE_REFRESH_MS` (the desk's lists, counts and open record), `WORKER_REFRESH_MS` (integration health and migration batches, which move with the worker) or `RUN_PROGRESS_REFRESH_MS` (a batch while it runs) from `lib/refresh.ts`. A new cadence is a named constant there with its reason.
  YES: `useConnectorHealthQuery(undefined, { pollingInterval: WORKER_REFRESH_MS, refetchOnFocus: true })`. NO: `pollingInterval: 15000`, or a `setInterval` that calls `refetch`.
- When the record itself decides whether to poll, read it from the cache first with the endpoint's `useQueryState`, which does not subscribe, and pass the interval to the query: `pollingInterval: running ? RUN_PROGRESS_REFRESH_MS : 0` in `app/(internal)/admin/migration/[id]/page.tsx`.
- An interval may tick a local clock and nothing else: `SlaValue`, the SLA rail and the SLA table count down at `SLA_TICK_MS` between polls.

## The server is the only author

- Never compute an SLA due time, a breach, a derived priority, burn-down, remaining capacity, a budget status or a permission in the browser. Render the value the API sent.
- When a figure needs its basis to be read correctly, put the basis in the label ("Remaining of plan" in `CapacityGrid`), never a recomputation.
- A figure the API did not send is left out, tile and panel both, never printed as zero.
  YES: `row.n === undefined ? null : <span className="xms-mono">{row.n}</span>`. NO: `{row.n ?? 0}`.
